Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:11:18

Release 0.5.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 04:25:06

Added. Native Vulkan kernels for HLX DLSS (owner, 20-11-2026: an option, off by default): a box beside Version on the
Setup page, remembered, adds --vulkan to HelixSR 3's builder, so Vulkan games run HLX DLSS in Vulkan instead of
through HelixSR Scaler's DirectX 12 bridge; the build then takes about twice as long. The Overview reads from the
builder's helixsr_setup.json whether the payload has them, and Download and build no longer calls a HelixSR 3 payload
current when Scaler's network or the Vulkan kernels asked for are missing. HelixSR 2's builder gets no --vulkan.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 04:19:27

Fixed. The Overview hashes a file once while its size and time stay the same (HelixSR 3's DLLs are 58 MB and more).

Changelog: 20-11-2026 04:19:27

Added. HelixSR Scaler for the games without FSR 3.1 (owner, 20-11-2026: in place of the stand-alone folder for
OptiScaler, with a HelixSR 3 payload). For 3.x Download and build also builds HLX DLSS's network into the release's
HelixSR/helixsr.dll with HelixSR's own builder (--no-fg); when that build fails HLX FSR 4 is ready all the same and
the Setup page says why. The whole release stays in the payload, as hard links where it can. The Deploy page's HelixSR
Scaler mode installs it next to the game's .exe with HelixSR's own installer (its bridge, setup/helixsr_bridge.py, as
HelixSR Desktop runs it): as dxgi.dll, or under another name when the game has its own, with the Steam launch option
then copied to the clipboard; the game's files it replaces are kept, Remove puts them back, Update older games brings
a newer HelixSR in and keeps the game's OptiScaler.ini. The Overview reads its state from HelixSR Scaler's install
record and HLX DLSS in the game.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 03:55:56

Added. HelixSR 3 (owner, 20-11-2026: HLX FSR 4 is the default for a game with FSR 3.1). The app sets up HelixSR up to
3.x (known 3.4.1). For 3.x Download and build downloads the release, checked against GitHub's SHA-256, and imports HLX
FSR 4 from its HLX-FSR4 folder, which comes built with its network inside. Replace the game's DLL puts HLX FSR 4 in
under the game's file name, the game's file kept as .original.dll as HelixSR's own installer does, and takes away
network files and a helixsr.ini an earlier HelixSR left there; Remove also deletes HLX FSR 4's HLX_FSR.log and
HLX_FSR_skip.txt. A game deployed with HelixSR 1 or 2 shows Older build, Update older games puts HLX FSR 4 in, and
Remove works as before. The Overview shows an HLX FSR 4 payload as such. The stand-alone folder for OptiScaler needs a
HelixSR 1 or 2 payload (the fallback on the Setup page); with HelixSR 3 its Deploy is off and says why.

